  "dom_id": "step-q92002",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "William read $72$ pages of a best-selling novel in $3$ hours. There is a proportional relationship between time $x$ William spends reading (in hours) and the number of pages $y$ he reads. What is the equation that represents the relationship between $x$ and $y?$",
  "worked_solution": "Every proportional relationship takes the form $y=kx,$ where $k$ is the constant of proportionality.\n\nWe are told that William read $y=72$ pages of the novel in $x=3$ hours.\n\nWe can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-value to the $x$-value, as follows:\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{72}{3}=24\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation is\n\n$$\ny=24x.\n$$",
